# JavaScript security (repave)

**Scope:** all **`.js` / `.mjs` / `.cjs`** in this repository. Run **`make js-lint`** before push (ESLint recommended + security rules).

## XSS and DOM

- **Avoid `innerHTML`** with dynamic or storage-backed strings (`sessionStorage`, user input, API JSON). Prefer **`textContent`**, **`createElement`**, or **`insertAdjacentText`**.
- When HTML is unavoidable, use a vetted escape helper or server-rendered static markup only — never concatenate untrusted data into tags or attributes.
- URL paths: use **`encodeURIComponent`** for path segments (see last-run / resume links).
- **`JSON.parse`**: only on trusted or size-bounded text; always **try/catch**; never parse cross-origin responses without validation.

## Execution and supply chain

- **No `eval`**, **`new Function`**, or **`setTimeout(string)`**.
- Portal static assets: **no third-party script tags** and no loading remote JS — keep logic in **`repave.js`** (CSP-friendly).
- Do not embed secrets, tokens, or session keys in client-side source.

## Browser storage and clipboard

- **sessionStorage / localStorage**: store non-sensitive UI state only (draft form fields, last-run metadata). Do not persist auth tokens in the browser.
- **Clipboard API**: use **`navigator.clipboard.writeText`** with rejection handled; copy **text**, not HTML.

## HTTP (if extended)

- Prefer same-origin form POSTs (current portal). Any future **`fetch`**: set explicit timeouts, avoid sending cookies to untrusted URLs, validate JSON shape before use.

## CI

ESLint runs in **Python quality and security** when `ci_needed` is true (see **`eslint.config.js`**).
